        "original_id": "790a506d-690d-5831-a5f7-42f072a15142",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Der Freischütz, Il trovatore\n- People: Carl Maria von Weber, Friedrich Kind, Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, spoken dialogue, acts, translation, adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the 1836 play \"El trovador,\" which later served as the basis for Il trovatore.\n- Der Freischütz, Op. 77, J. 277, is a German opera with spoken dialogue in three acts by Carl Maria von Weber and a libretto by Friedrich Kind.\n- Der Freischütz is usually translated as \"The Marksman\" or \"The Freeshooter.\"\n- Il trovatore is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano.\n- Il trovatore means \"The Troubadour\" in Italian.\n- Il trovatore is based on Antonio García Gutiérrez's play \"El trovador.\"",
